                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "The fourth installment of the Blackwell saga. This was the biggest game in the series of the four I have played so far. I dare say that this game improves upon just about everything from the previous games, ranging from interface to story and the ratio between answered questions and loose ends that keep the mystery interesting.\n\nAfter finishing the third game, I was hoping for a merging of the \"combining notes mechanic\" from Legacy with the free text input from Unbound and Convergence to appear in a later game. We got just that in this game. Rosa have the abillity to free text search with Oogle on her phone as well as combining clues in her notes to form new clues. I liked the combination of both systems we got in this game.\n\nFinishing this game made me even more excited to play the fifth and last chapter.",
